          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-ink">Business Layer</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">Business strategy, goals, objectives, operating models, value streams, and stakeholder concerns. The business layer defines the context and requirements for all other architecture layers.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper p-6" data-reveal>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <span class="flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-accent-soft text-sm font-semibold text-accent">02</span>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-ink">Capability Layer</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">Business capabilities, capability maturity levels, and the mapping of capabilities to business strategy, processes, applications, and technology. The bridge between business and IT.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper p-6" data-reveal>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <span class="flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-accent-soft text-sm font-semibold text-accent">03</span>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-ink">Process Layer</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">Business processes, workflows, procedures, and process ownership. Process models define how business capabilities are delivered and how applications and data support them.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper p-6" data-reveal>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <span class="flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-accent-soft text-sm font-semibold text-accent">04</span>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-ink">Application Layer</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">Application portfolio, application interfaces, application services, and application interactions. Defines what applications exist, what they do, and how they relate to business capabilities.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper p-6" data-reveal>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <span class="flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-accent-soft text-sm font-semibold text-accent">05</span>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-ink">Data Layer</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">Data entities, data domains, data products, data stores, data flows, data governance, and data lifecycle management. Defines how data is created, stored, shared, and retired.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper p-6" data-reveal>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <span class="flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-accent-soft text-sm font-semibold text-accent">06</span>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-ink">Integration Layer</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">APIs, event brokers, integration platforms, service mesh, and integration patterns. Defines how applications and data services communicate across the enterprise.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper p-6" data-reveal>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <span class="flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-accent-soft text-sm font-semibold text-accent">07</span>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-ink">Platform Layer</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">Internal platforms, developer platforms, API platforms, data platforms, and AI platforms. Shared infrastructure and services that enable consistent, self-service delivery.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper p-6" data-reveal>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <span class="flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-accent-soft text-sm font-semibold text-accent">08</span>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-ink">Infrastructure Layer</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">Compute, storage, networking, data centers, cloud resources, and edge infrastructure. The physical and virtual foundation that supports all other layers.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper p-6" data-reveal>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <span class="flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-accent-soft text-sm font-semibold text-accent">09</span>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-ink">Security Layer</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">Security controls, identity and access management, encryption, threat detection, compliance monitoring, and security governance. Cross-cutting across all other layers.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper p-6 md:col-span-2 lg:col-span-3" data-reveal>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <span class="flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-accent-soft text-sm font-semibold text-accent">10</span>
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-ink">Governance Layer</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">Architecture principles, technology standards, architecture review processes, decision records (ADRs), reference architectures, and compliance monitoring. Governance is the cross-cutting layer that ensures all other layers remain aligned, consistent, and strategically directed.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

