<!-- 14. FAQ -->
<section class="py-20 md:py-28 bg-graphite" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
  <div class="container-x">
    <SectionHeading
      id="faq-heading"
      index="14"
      label="Frequently Asked Questions"
      title="Common questions about Enterprise Architecture."
      lede="Answers to the questions we hear most often from executives and architects evaluating Enterprise Architecture engagement."
      tone="graphite"
    />
    <div class="mt-14 max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-4" data-reveal-group>
      
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 open:border-accent-bright transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-graphite-fg list-none">
          What is Enterprise Architecture?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-graphite-fg-3 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">Enterprise Architecture is the practice of analyzing, designing, planning, and governing the enterprise technology ecosystem to ensure it supports business strategy. It provides a holistic view of capabilities, processes, applications, data, and infrastructure, and establishes the standards and roadmaps that guide technology decisions.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 open:border-accent-bright transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-graphite-fg list-none">
          What is the difference between Enterprise Architecture and Solution Architecture?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-graphite-fg-3 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">Enterprise Architecture operates at the organizational level, defining strategic direction, standards, and principles. Solution Architecture operates at the project level, designing specific systems within the enterprise context. EA sets the rules; SA plays within them.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 open:border-accent-bright transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-graphite-fg list-none">
          What is the difference between Enterprise Architecture and Software Architecture?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-graphite-fg-3 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">Software Architecture focuses on the internal structure of software systems: components, modules, interfaces, and design patterns. Enterprise Architecture covers business processes, data flows, application portfolios, infrastructure, and their interrelationships across the entire organization.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 open:border-accent-bright transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-graphite-fg list-none">
          What is TOGAF and why does it matter?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-graphite-fg-3 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">TOGAF (The Open Group Architecture Framework) is the industry-standard framework for developing and governing enterprise architectures. It provides the Architecture Development Method (ADM), architecture content framework, and capability framework. We apply TOGAF pragmatically, adapting it to each organizations context.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 open:border-accent-bright transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-graphite-fg list-none">
          Do we need TOGAF certification to practice Enterprise Architecture?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-graphite-fg-3 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">No. While TOGAF provides a useful framework and vocabulary, many organizations practice effective Enterprise Architecture without formal certification. We adapt the framework to your maturity level. The goal is architecture outcomes, not framework compliance.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 open:border-accent-bright transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-graphite-fg list-none">
          How long does an Enterprise Architecture engagement take?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-graphite-fg-3 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">A focused architecture assessment typically takes 4 to 8 weeks. A full architecture transformation including strategy, roadmap, and governance setup takes 3 to 6 months. Ongoing architecture advisory continues as the practice matures.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 open:border-accent-bright transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-graphite-fg list-none">
          What does an Architecture Review Board do?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-graphite-fg-3 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">An Architecture Review Board evaluates solution architectures for alignment with enterprise standards, principles, and strategic direction. It provides governance, identifies risks, approves or rejects exceptions, and ensures consistency across the technology portfolio.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 open:border-accent-bright transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-graphite-fg list-none">
          What is a technology roadmap and how is it created?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-graphite-fg-3 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">A technology roadmap is a strategic plan that maps current-state to future-state architecture over time. It is created by analyzing the gap between current and target architecture, prioritizing initiatives based on business value and dependencies, and sequencing work into phased delivery waves.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 open:border-accent-bright transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-graphite-fg list-none">
          How does cloud transformation relate to Enterprise Architecture?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-graphite-fg-3 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">Cloud transformation touches every EA domain: application architecture, data architecture, security architecture, integration architecture, and governance. EA provides the framework for a coherent cloud strategy.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 open:border-accent-bright transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-graphite-fg list-none">
          How do you approach legacy system modernization?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-graphite-fg-3 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">We assess legacy systems on business value and technical condition, then select the appropriate strategy: retain, retire, replace, rehost, replatform, refactor, or rebuild. We use incremental patterns like strangler fig and parallel run to reduce risk.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 open:border-accent-bright transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-graphite-fg list-none">
          What is business capability mapping?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-graphite-fg-3 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">Business capability mapping identifies and categorizes what the business does (its capabilities), not how it does it (its processes). Capabilities are organized in a hierarchical map that shows the relationship between business functions and supporting technology systems.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 open:border-accent-bright transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-graphite-fg list-none">
          What is a reference architecture?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-graphite-fg-3 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">A reference architecture is a reusable architecture template for a common pattern or domain. Examples include microservice reference architecture, event-driven reference architecture, data mesh reference architecture, and cloud landing zone reference architecture.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 open:border-accent-bright transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-graphite-fg list-none">
          How does Enterprise Architecture handle data?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-graphite-fg-3 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">Data architecture within EA covers data domains, data products, data stores, data flows, data governance, master data management, metadata management, and data lifecycle policies. A well-designed data architecture eliminates silos and enables analytics and AI initiatives.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 open:border-accent-bright transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-graphite-fg list-none">
          How does security fit into Enterprise Architecture?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-graphite-fg-3 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">Security architecture is an integral EA domain. It defines security principles, controls, identity and access management, encryption standards, network security, threat detection, and compliance frameworks. Security is designed into every architecture layer.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 open:border-accent-bright transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-graphite-fg list-none">
          How do you measure Enterprise Architecture success?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-graphite-fg-3 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">We measure EA success through business outcomes: reduced IT costs, faster time to market, improved integration success rates, reduced technical debt, higher architecture compliance, and faster cloud migration velocity.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 open:border-accent-bright transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-graphite-fg list-none">
          What is the difference between EA and IT strategy?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-graphite-fg-3 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">IT strategy defines what the organization will achieve with technology and why. Enterprise Architecture defines how the technology landscape is structured to deliver that strategy. IT strategy sets direction; EA provides the blueprint and governance.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 open:border-accent-bright transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-graphite-fg list-none">
          How do you implement architecture governance without slowing teams?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-graphite-fg-3 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">Good governance accelerates delivery. We implement lightweight, risk-based review processes where low-risk changes follow automated or expedited paths. Clear standards reduce decision overhead. Reference architectures provide ready-made templates.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 open:border-accent-bright transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-graphite-fg list-none">
          How does Enterprise Architecture support digital transformation?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-graphite-fg-3 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">Enterprise Architecture provides the strategic context, current-state understanding, future-state vision, and transformation roadmap that make digital transformation achievable. Without EA, transformation initiatives lack coherence and direction.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 open:border-accent-bright transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-graphite-fg list-none">
          When should an organization start practicing Enterprise Architecture?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-graphite-fg-3 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">The right time is when technology complexity begins to slow the business. Symptoms include rising IT costs, integration challenges, slow project delivery, and inconsistent technology choices. Starting early is better than waiting for a crisis.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 open:border-accent-bright transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-[1rem] font-medium text-graphite-fg list-none">
          How do you ensure architecture decisions are followed?
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-graphite-fg-3 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5">
          <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2 leading-relaxed">Through lightweight governance, clear communication of value, and embedding architects in delivery teams. Architecture standards are enforced through automated checks in CI/CD pipelines, not through gatekeeping or manual approvals.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

